I arrive at the hairdresser at half past four.
I am always punctual.
The hairdresser greets me.
She washes and cuts my hair.
It takes about an hour.
My new hair is very nice.
I thank the hairdresser and leave the salon.
My bike is out front.
I cycle through the city.
It is Thursday evening.
I cycle to a cozy cafe.
I park my bike and go inside.
Nina is already sitting at a table.
I look at my watch.
It is exactly six o'clock.
"Hi Maya, your hair is really nice," Nina says.
"Thank you very much," I say.
We order two cups of coffee.
We drink the coffee and chat together.
I always enjoy our coffee dates.
